142:  * Which way the wind blows, on the ground, as a unit vector in world xz.
143:  *
144:  * The leaves have always blown along -x (the recipe below, from the
145:  * original's own emitter). Exported because the grass has to lean the same
146:  * way: a field whose waves cross it in one direction while the leaves over
147:  * it fly in another is the kind of disagreement nobody can name but everyone
148:  * sees. One wind, two readers.
149:  */
150: export const GROUND_WIND: readonly [number, number] = [-1, 0];
