165: /**
166:  * The model's own folder is where the original looks and where the texture
167:  * almost always is. A handful of BMDs name a file that this data tree keeps
168:  * somewhere else: `Skill/Rider01.bmd` (the Uniria) asks for `unicon.jpg`,
169:  * which ships as `Data/Item/unicon.OZJ`, and the three pets of
170:  * `Data/Player/Helper0n.bmd` ask for `fairy` / `satan` the same way. Those
171:  * came out untextured, which for a model this runtime draws unlit is a solid
172:  * white silhouette - a mount and its rider lighting up the screen.
173:  *
174:  * So: fall back to the file name across the whole tree. The original does the
175:  * same - `CLoadData::OpenTexture` (LoadData.cpp:100-108) hands the bare name
176:  * to `CGlobalBitmap::FindTextureByName` and takes whatever bitmap is already
177:  * loaded under it, which means load order decides when a name ships more than
178:  * once. Load order is not worth copying, so: most of these are byte-identical
179:  * wherever they sit and the copy is taken outright; the handful that differ go
180:  * by `FOLDER_ORDER`, and every one of those picks is logged.
