228: 
229:   // MU packs a texture in the container matching the format the BMD names,
230:   // and the extension is load-bearing: `.tga` means the 32-bit `.OZT`, which
231:   // carries the alpha key, and `.jpg`/`.bmp` mean the 24-bit `.OZJ`, which
232:   // has no alpha channel at all. The same base name usually ships as *both*.
233:   //
234:   // Searching OZJ-first regardless threw that away. `Grass03.bmd` asks for
235:   // `tree_01.tga` and got `tree_01.OZJ` - a 128x64 opaque JPEG in place of a
236:   // 32x32 cut-out - while the mesh stayed marked transparent by the `.tga`
237:   // test further down. An alpha-tested card whose alpha is a solid 1.0 draws
238:   // as a full rectangle, which is Lorencia's planter bushes and Devias' trees
239:   // rendering as flat grey pleated cards.
240:   //
241:   // Only textures shipping as both were affected, which is why the damage
242:   // looked arbitrary: `Grass01`/`Grass02` use `tree_08`, which has no `.OZJ`,
243:   // and came out correct through the same broken ordering.
244:   const ext = texPath.slice(texPath.lastIndexOf('.')).toLowerCase();
245: 
246:   const OZT: [string, number][] = [['.OZT', 4]];
247: 
248:   const OZJ: [string, number][] = [['.OZJ', 24]];
249: 
250:   // The non-matching container is still tried, last: a missing texture is a
251:   // worse outcome than an opaque one, and this is the only reason the wrong
252:   // ordering went unnoticed.
